        {
            "id": "com.polyphase.build.target.linux-arm64",
            "name": "Linux ARM64",
            "summary": "Linux ARM64 build target.",
            "description": "Adds a 'Linux ARM64 (aarch64)' build target to the Polyphase editor. Cross-compiles the existing Linux + Vulkan game runtime (PLATFORM_LINUX=1, API_VULKAN=1) via aarch64-linux-gnu-* against a user-provided ARM64 sysroot, and emits an ARM64 ELF runnable on Debian/Ubuntu-class aarch64 devices (Orange Pi 5, Pine64, Raspberry Pi 4/5 with Mesa Vulkan, etc.). On Linux/macOS the toolchain runs natively; on Windows it runs inside WSL2 (aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc ships in apt as crossbuild-essential-arm64). Build outputs go to Build/Linux/arm64/ and Intermediate/Linux/arm64/ so they never collide with x64 Linux builds (relies on the engine's BUILD_SUFFIX makefile variable).",
